message: "Please cite this dated overview when referring to its selected experimental results."
title: "DE10-Nano active noise cancellation: public overview and selected evidence"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Thomson
    given-names: Neil
version: "2026.11.22"
date-released: 2026-11-22
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pealie/de10-nano-anc-overview"
url: "https://github.com/Pealie/de10-nano-anc-overview"
abstract: "Three 60-second matched pairs across two board boots achieved 5.64, 6.15 and 5.70 dB attenuation of a tracked tone near 200 Hz at one marked RIGHT microphone position. All 180 one-second intervals exceeded 3 dB. The public evidence also preserves the two earlier experiments from 4–5 November 2026 and their original scores."
keywords:
  - active noise cancellation
  - FPGA
  - DE10-Nano
  - digital signal processing
  - adaptive feedback
  - reproducible measurements
